  "description": {
    "raw": "This spell allows you to turn a potion into a temporary pool of necromantic energy. Only a potion created using a conjuration (healing) spell can be affected by this spell. An affected potion turns dark red and reveals a necromantic aura if detect magic is cast on it while it remains under this spell’s effects.\n\nWhen you drink a potion affected by this spell, you do not gain the potion’s normal effect. Instead, the first necromancy spell you cast within the next minute is cast at a higher caster level. The bonus to caster level is equal to the spell level of the spell used to create the potion that deathwine affects. For example, a 5th-level wizard who drinks deathwine made from a potion of cure serious wounds would cast his next necromancy spell as an 8th-level caster, as cure serious wounds is a 3rd-level spell.\n\nIn addition, any undead creature (or other creature healed by negative energy) that drinks a potion affected by deathwine is healed of 1d8 points of damage. Any potion not imbibed before this spell’s duration expires is destroyed at the end of the deathwine’s duration.",
    "search_text": "\"this spell allows you to turn a potion into a temporary pool of necromantic energy. only a potion created using a conjuration (healing) spell can be affected by this spell. an affected potion turns dark red and reveals a necromantic aura if detect magic is cast on it while it remains under this spell’s effects.\\n\\nwhen you drink a potion affected by this spell, you do not gain the potion’s normal effect. instead, the first necromancy spell you cast within the next minute is cast at a higher caster level. the bonus to caster level is equal to the spell level of the spell used to create the potion that deathwine affects. for example, a 5th-level wizard who drinks deathwine made from a potion of cure serious wounds would cast his next necromancy spell as an 8th-level caster, as cure serious wounds is a 3rd-level spell.\\n\\nin addition, any undead creature (or other creature healed by negative energy) that drinks a potion affected by deathwine is healed of 1d8 points of damage. any potion not imbibed before this spell’s duration expires is destroyed at the end of the deathwine’s duration.\"",
    "sections": []
  },
